  "matchDatasources": [
    "apk"
  ],
  "matchUpdateTypes": [
    "patch"
  ],
  "groupName": "apk pkgrel pin bumps",
  "groupSlug": "apk-pkgrel",
  "schedule": [
    "after 8pm on sunday",
    "before 8am on monday"
  ],
  "automerge": true,
  "automergeStrategy": "rebase"
},
{
  "description": "apk pkgver bumps (upstream version changes) may change CLI semantics – cf. hd-idle-genargs – so they keep human review: label and leave automerge off (patch bumps automerge via the previous rule). Grouped like the patch rule: one reviewed release per pkgver event, all drifted pins in one self-consistent tree.",
  "matchDatasources": [
    "apk"
  ],
  "matchUpdateTypes": [
    "minor",
    "major"
  ],
  "groupName": "apk pkgver pin bumps",
  "groupSlug": "apk-pkgver",
  "schedule": [
    "after 8pm on sunday",
    "before 8am on monday"
  ],
  "addLabels": [
    "needs-review"
  ]
},
{
  "description": "GitHub Actions: weekly",
  "matchManagers": [
    "github-actions"
  ],
  "addLabels": [
    "github_actions"
  ],
  "schedule": [
    "after 8pm on sunday",
    "before 8am on monday"
  ]
},
{
  "description": "Our own actions that follow a branch (like home-assistant/actions@master) float on purpose. Pinning them would open a digest PR in every repository for each change to them. Our own actions on a version tag are pinned like any other.",
  "matchManagers": [
    "github-actions"
  ],
  "matchPackageNames": [
    "home-assistant/**"
  ],
  "matchCurrentValue": "/^(dev|main|master)$/",
  "pinDigests": false
},
{
  "description": "mise [tools] pins (mise manager; registry-backed: github/aqua/npm/core backends): weekly, same cadence as the actions manager. Renovate updates the pinned version and runs `mise lock` in safe mode so mise.lock stays in sync; the CI check job (hk lint gate + validate) validates the bumped toolset before merge.",
  "matchManagers": [
    "mise"
  ],
  "addLabels": [
    "mise_tools"
  ],
  "schedule": [
    "after 8pm on sunday",
    "before 8am on monday"
  ]
},
{
  "description": "hk pkl-package manager (custom.regex): same weekly Monday cadence and label as the mise [tools] rule so BOTH hk deps of the pair update together (mise manager owns mise.toml + mise.lock, this one hk.pkl) – a schedule mismatch would open one-sided desync PRs on off-Monday runs. Listed for both match spellings because the mise manager's dep matches packageRules by its resolved packageName jdx/hk, not the depName hk that PR titles show (verified against Renovate 44.235.0, 2026-11-12, local reproduction), and which side wins for custom-manager deps is not pinned down.",
  "matchManagers": [
    "custom.regex"
  ],
  "matchPackageNames": [
    "hk",
    "jdx/hk"
  ],
  "addLabels": [
    "mise_tools"
  ],
  "schedule": [
    "after 8pm on sunday",
    "before 8am on monday"
  ]
},
{
  "description": "Supervisor schema pin: weekly batch cadence (same schedule strip as the tool/action rules), so the whole dependency batch opens Sunday evening and is merged before Monday 8am. The Renovate PR body lists the upstream changelog for an audit trail. Merged by GitHub's native auto-merge once branch protection's required checks are green (platformAutomerge; see repository-root KNOWLEDGE.md §\"CI: Branch protection and platform-native automerge\"). automergeStrategy rebase: linear history, one conventional commit per bump (GitHub replays the branch's single commit onto the tip at merge time); conflicts block the merge until Renovate rebases – same as manual.",
  "matchManagers": [
    "custom.regex"
  ],
  "addLabels": [
    "supervisor_pin"
  ],
  "schedule": [
    "after 8pm on sunday",
    "before 8am on monday"
  ],
  "automerge": true,
  "automergeStrategy": "rebase"
},
{
  "description": "Automerge minor and patch mise [tools] bumps once CI is green: the PR's check job runs the lint gate plus validate:apps on the toolset it installs, so green certifies the eagerly-installed tools against the repo exactly as they will run after merge – a release that newly fires rules fails the bump PR's own gate instead of landing, and later PRs run the same gate, so nothing slips through post-merge. mise-action's bare install skips lazy-declared tools (copilot, go, the go:-backend agent, vendir) – their bumps ride on the install's lockfile gate (mise-action adds --locked when a lockfile is present, so a mise.toml/mise.lock desync fails the check) rather than on tool execution. Majors keep human review: they can redefine semantics the config was verified against (hk's hk.pkl contract, renovate config flags, runtime majors like node/python/go).",
  "matchManagers": [
    "mise"
  ],
  "matchUpdateTypes": [
    "minor",
    "patch"
  ],
  "automerge": true,
  "automergeStrategy": "rebase"
},
{
  "description": "Automerge minor and patch hk bumps for the mise-custom pair: Renovate folds mise.toml, mise.lock and hk.pkl into one branch anyway, and the check job runs hk itself – a green PR certifies the bumped hk plus the desync invariant (mise install --locked). Majors keep human review – hk majors may redefine the hk.pkl step contract this repo's lint gate is built on.",
  "matchManagers": [
    "custom.regex"
  ],
  "matchPackageNames": [

